<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-asia</id><updated>2026-09-29T14:56:02Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-asia" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-12758?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-asia" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>North Korea has recently completed two road bridges easing transport to strategic allies Russia and China</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:32b6364eb60b241f4a1c766784daed2445f33576d15b276e8ac8ec1b69d3ac36</id><updated>2026-09-29T14:55:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-29T13:35:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/north-korea-has-recently-completed-two-road-bridges-easing-transport-to-strategic-allies-russia-and-/a-79473981--09998bc65869.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/north-korea-has-recently-completed-two-road-bridges-easing-transport-to-strategic-allies-russia-and-china/a-79473981?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Two recently opened bridges are expected to ease trade and transport between North Korea and its powerful neighbors. The new connections come as Pyongyang builds strategic ties with China and Russia.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Women and children displaced by Nepal's floods say safe housing, privacy and stability remain out of reach as they try to rebuild their lives</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ae3f0b02e37b702af046f0b2b434d0214372570718592d22912b045d54c91255</id><updated>2026-09-29T14:55:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-29T13:29:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/women-and-children-displaced-by-nepal-s-floods-say-safe-housing-privacy-and-stability-remain-out-of-/a-79474014--3aa02594713a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/women-and-children-displaced-by-nepal-s-floods-say-safe-housing-privacy-and-stability-remain-out-of-reach-as-they-try-to-rebuild-their-lives/a-79474014?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Families living in temporary shelters in northern Nepal say safety and privacy remain out of reach as concerns about trafficking and abuse mount.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Malaysia repatriates Myanmar migrants despite UN warnings</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2b14f3b8e9cd840f67e34eb203b677e3ab2cded30704205e334f08536c55df8f</id><updated>2026-09-29T14:55:40Z</updated><published>2026-09-29T10:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/malaysia-repatriates-myanmar-migrants-despite-un-warnings/a-79470814--e0fb5ad7aea0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/malaysia-repatriates-myanmar-migrants-despite-un-warnings/a-79470814?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Malaysia has started repatriating about 1,500 Myanmar nationals, defying warnings from the UN and rights groups. Malaysia, facing an uptick in anti-migrant sentiment, says the program is strictly voluntary.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>US sanctions on Iran's aviation industry make travel less predictable as countries cancel flights</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:92d62f094e93ffa98af98ccdc60329f82d3aa20e387d49a184040e93e248b2b1</id><updated>2026-09-29T14:54:40Z</updated><published>2026-09-29T00:01:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-sanctions-on-iran-s-aviation-industry-make-travel-less-predictable-as-countries-cancel-flights/a-79459140--66d2076cb57a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-sanctions-on-iran-s-aviation-industry-make-travel-less-predictable-as-countries-cancel-flights/a-79459140?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The threat of secondary US sanctions is putting pressure on airports, fuel suppliers and aviation companies that service Iranian airlines. Some countries have already canceled flights.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>India's youth-led Cockroach movement targets election chief over voter-roll dispute</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3fd132166312e786f1a727aeb3acefbdbfc968c9246c5d52e1ed6804f6761fd5</id><updated>2026-09-29T14:56:02Z</updated><published>2026-09-28T14:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-s-youth-led-cockroach-movement-targets-election-chief-over-voter-roll-dispute/a-79462036--b918a132d9c5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-s-youth-led-cockroach-movement-targets-election-chief-over-voter-roll-dispute/a-79462036?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Cockroach movement has emerged as an influential force in Indian politics. Its latest campaign targets the election commission amid a wider debate over voter rolls and public trust in electoral institutions.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>India: LPU suspends classes after violent protests over alleged campus rape</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1229eef2cffa472a7434389a3600321f4af02d6c661388c3cb71e339ecffedf5</id><updated>2026-09-29T14:54:40Z</updated><published>2026-09-28T08:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-lpu-suspends-classes-after-violent-protests-over-alleged-campus-rape/live-79454038--f47bda72507a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-lpu-suspends-classes-after-violent-protests-over-alleged-campus-rape/live-79454038?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A university in Punjab has suspended classes after protests over a rumored sexual assault took a violent turn. Separately, the Supreme Court has taken suo motu cognizance of recent rape cases in Delhi.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine, South Korea relations sour over North Korean POWs</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3ee4fcc4cbab6a346a4f49c63cd20f1b225d8ca823e71bebeebb95fe02660f1d</id><updated>2026-09-29T14:54:40Z</updated><published>2026-09-28T02:32:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ukraine-south-korea-relations-sour-over-north-korean-pows/a-79451515--af4e1d864b6a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ukraine-south-korea-relations-sour-over-north-korean-pows/a-79451515?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">South Korea has accused Ukraine of breaching a confidentiality agreement over the transfer of North Korean prisoners of war — and of denying the deal's existence. Seoul has demanded an apology.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Avalanche in Nepal leaves 2 dead, several missing</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:59201c5ec651925471cb7f4e5658a2d5038c70b9850507c37e866f308fca56b7</id><updated>2026-09-29T14:54:40Z</updated><published>2026-09-27T17:47:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/avalanche-in-nepal-leaves-2-dead-several-missing/a-79450101--fcbca2d1e804.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/avalanche-in-nepal-leaves-2-dead-several-missing/a-79450101?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">An avalanche has struck the Himlung Himal base camp in Nepal after days of severe weather. Two guides are confirmed dead and at least 14 people remain missing in the remote region.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>South Korea's gender pay gap grows as women get older</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:34f87e0513bb8c948aa6e73881276f010d4ad7d2ef1e4ff3fce95fdc467df1d9</id><updated>2026-09-29T14:54:40Z</updated><published>2026-09-26T10:44:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/south-korea-s-gender-pay-gap-grows-as-women-get-older/a-79431285--9ddac1458d8e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/south-korea-s-gender-pay-gap-grows-as-women-get-older/a-79431285?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A new report shows how in South Korea, women on average earn less and have fewer employment opportunities throughout their lives.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>After Xi-Trump summit, US-China rivalry remains frozen. Is this to Beijing's advantage?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5064c641ea3faf02b5f9b4107e806ec206a73768167fabc8f9c9ed753cc555e5</id><updated>2026-09-29T14:54:40Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T11:35:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/after-xi-trump-summit-us-china-rivalry-remains-frozen-is-this-to-beijing-s-advantage/a-79427127--110c4fa9d052.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/after-xi-trump-summit-us-china-rivalry-remains-frozen-is-this-to-beijing-s-advantage/a-79427127?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The US president showcased White House construction projects and hosted a lavish dinner with tech CEOs, but the summit made little progress on key issues such as trade tensions and AI regulation.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Three-way battle for power in world chess: Who will be elected FIDE president in Samarkand?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:48601a0841cb6a0ed9185cbeccf6bcf0351c2e8e14ea6f0e8014f4319fa9e430</id><updated>2026-09-29T14:54:40Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T18:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/three-way-battle-for-power-in-world-chess-who-will-be-elected-fide-president-in-samarkand/a-79413301--bc60333e85fc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/three-way-battle-for-power-in-world-chess-who-will-be-elected-fide-president-in-samarkand/a-79413301?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The era of Russian presidents is coming to an end at the World Chess Federation (FIDE). Two Germans and one Kazakh are up for election. Among the issues at play are money, Kremlin influence, and unanswered questions.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Pakistan: Khan family arrests raise stakes ahead of protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fc8462ab4856a8487847b28c8c7ce80256762ba997c4825369fef2df46d1a977</id><updated>2026-09-29T14:54:40Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T13:39:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/pakistan-khan-family-arrests-raise-stakes-ahead-of-protests/a-79392147--cb3db8a0de02.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/pakistan-khan-family-arrests-raise-stakes-ahead-of-protests/a-79392147?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The sons of Pakistan's jailed former Prime Minister Imran Khan told DW their father is in ill health while being isolated from family and doctors. Other relatives have been detained ahead of a planned opposition protest.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Nepal rejects 'sympathy,' asks for $20 million after floods</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9f6982eb2bffaf4ac57472156c879fb8afee172993ba510214deca7333d1b183</id><updated>2026-09-29T14:54:40Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T12:37:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nepal-rejects-sympathy-asks-for-20-mill-after-floods/a-79372239--b0482f9bc73a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nepal-rejects-sympathy-asks-for-20-million-after-floods/a-79372239?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">With Nepal still reeling from the devastating floods in August, Kathmandu is calling for climate justice and seeking compensation from the UN-backed Loss and Damage Fund, Environment Minister Geeta Chaudhary told DW.</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
